 "day": 8,
 "topic": "App startup time",
 "tag": "MOBILE-PERF",
 "script": {
  "hook": "Users tap your icon and stare at a blank splash for four seconds.",
  "question": "Design a fast app startup.",
  "trap": "The trap: initialize every SDK at launch. Analytics, ads and crash tools block the first frame, so the app feels dead.",
  "steps": [
   "Measure cold start. Process start to first frame, on a mid range device, as a percentile.",
   "Defer the work. Only the first screen is allowed on the critical path. Lazy init the rest, after the first frame or on a background thread.",
   "Cheap first frame. Show a cached layout right away, skip heavy inflation, load fresh data after.",
   "Precompile the hot path. Baseline profiles on Android skip slow first run code. On iOS, cut dynamic frameworks and static initializers."
  ],
  "takeaway": "Do less before the first frame, and measure it every release.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: deep links.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
